<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolków Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolków Castle stands above the town of Bolków in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-silesia">Lower Silesia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. It was built in the late 13th century by Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolko-i-the-strict">Bolko I the Strict</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swidnica">Świdnica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawor">Jawor</a> to guard the routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. Rebuilt in the 16th century, it fell into ruin after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, but its tall keep survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolkow-castle.jpg" alt="Bolków Castle" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacek Halicki · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2018_Zamek_w_Bolkowie_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
